     7	## Bottom line
     8	
     9	The reported disagreement is real, but it combines two cases:
    10	
    11	1. The large disagreement is not two implementations of the same integral. A `StepEvaluator` configured with `boundary_indices=(0,)` sends that subset only through `evaluate_many`; `evaluate` ignores it, materializes all 48 tape boundaries, and integrates the full trajectory. Dense boundary 0 is explicitly held for 30.08 s. This is the exact primary mechanism.
    12	2. With both paths on all 48 boundaries, realised-field parity is numerical but never fully binary64-identical in this sample. Nominal-field parity also has five threshold-sensitive outliers (maximum 0.02041 κ), which the present synthetic approximate-parity KAT does not expose.
