    64	- `evaluate` never reads `self.boundary_indices`; it calls `tape.geometry_for` (`run_v025_matrix_probe.py:903-912`). `geometry_for` unconditionally iterates `range(step.boundary_count)` (`src/mcrl/physics_v025/tapes.py:860-879`), and the scalar adapter requires exactly 48 boundaries (`src/mcrl/physics_v025/adapter.py:98-127`) before the 47-subinterval trapezoid (`src/mcrl/physics_v025/integration.py:165-185`). The probe recorded 48 evaluations from 0 to 30.08 s.
    65	- Cache state makes the semantic split sticky: `_evaluated` is keyed only by `configuration_id`, and `evaluate_many` skips already-cached IDs (`run_v025_matrix_probe.py:788-797`). A scalar-cached reference therefore survives a later batch call.
