-## S0 decision inventory
-
-### Decision object and candidate formation
-
-**Verified.** At each of 120 authenticated E1 predecision anchors, the decoder chooses one complete 100-user action vector. `S0` chooses over:
-
-1. one BASE vector, the masked first-index argmax of frozen float32 `Q1+Q2`;
-2. every legal, non-NOOP, physically non-equivalent single-user edit, with all other users fixed to BASE; and
-3. every saved “evacuate one whole BASE-served origin beam to one commonly legal non-origin physical destination” vector.
-
-`S0-U` permits only (1)+(2); `S0-J` permits only (1)+(3). The S0 runner constructs rows from the E1 tape at [run_probe_s0.py:398](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-c3s-run/.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3-probe-s0/run_probe_s0.py:398) and applies the three allowed-kind sets at [run_probe_s0.py:543](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-c3s-run/.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3-probe-s0/run_probe_s0.py:543). E1's exhaustive unilateral rule and full-origin evacuation rule are declared at [run_v023_c3_existence_e1.py:259](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-c3s-run/.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3-existence-e1/run_v023_c3_existence_e1.py:259), with evacuation enumeration implemented at [run_v023_c3_existence_e1.py:826](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-c3s-run/.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3-existence-e1/run_v023_c3_existence_e1.py:826).
